  "finalReply": "Done. React peer conflicts are resolved and everything installs and builds cleanly.\n\n**Root cause:** `@monorepo/ui-lib` declared `react/react-dom ^17.0.0` peers (and React 17 dev deps + `@types/react` 17) while `app` (`^18.2.0`) and `docs` (`^18.3.0`) consumed React 18. `npm ls` showed two React copies (17.0.2 + 18.3.1) and `app`/`docs` builds failed with `TS2322` type mismatches between `@types/react` 17 and 18.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added `fix-react-conflicts.js` (run with `node fix-react-conflicts.js`; supports `--root <dir>`, `--skip-install`): discovers workspace `package.json` files, validates existence/JSON before touching anything, detects mismatched React majors, aligns all `react`/`react-dom` specs to the highest found version and `@types/react(-dom)` majors to match, then verifies with `npm install`. Exit 0 on resolved/no-conflict, exit 1 with no file modifications on missing/invalid JSON or unparseable (unresolvable) specs.\n- Ran it: aligned `ui-lib` peers + dev `react/react-dom` `^17.x` → `^18.3.0`, `@types/react(-dom)` `^17.0.0` → `^18.0.0`, and `app` `react/react-dom` `^18.2.0` → `^18.3.0` (highest version). `docs` already `^18.3.0`, untouched.\n\n**Verification performed:**\n- First run: applied 7 updates, `npm install` inside the script succeeded, exit 0.\n- Re-run: `No React peer dependency conflicts detected (react major: 18). No changes made.`, exit 0.\n- `npm install`: clean, exit 0, no vulnerabilities.\n- `npm run build --workspaces`: all 3 packages compile, exit 0 (previously `app`/`docs` failed).\n- `npm ls react --all`: single deduped `react@18.3.1` everywhere.\n- Edge probes in temp dirs: invalid JSON → exit 1, file untouched; missing file → exit 1; unparseable spec → exit 1 with details, files untouched; no-conflict → exit 0; resolvable conflict → exit 0 with fix applied.",
